'''''Placopleurus''''' is an [[extinct]] [[genus]] of prehistoric [[ray-finned fish]] from the [[Middle Triassic]] [[epoch (geology)|epoch]] ([[Anisian]] and [[Ladinian]] [[stage (geology)|stages]]) of Italy, Slovenia, and Switzerland.<ref name="sepkoskidb">{{cite journal |last=Sepkoski |first=Jack |title=A compendium of fossil marine animal genera |journal=Bulletins of American Paleontology |volume=364 |page=560 |date=2002 |url=http://strata.ummp.lsa.umich.edu/jack/showgenera.php?taxon=611&rank=class |accessdate=2009-02-27}}</ref><ref name="Bürgin1992">{{cite journal |last=Bürgin |first=Toni |year=1992 |title=Basal ray-finned fishes (Osteichthyes; Actinopterygii) from the Middle Triassic of Monte San Giorgio (Canton Tessin, Switzerland). Systematic palaeontology with notes on functional morphology and palaeoecology |journal=Schweizerische Paläontologische Abhandlungen |volume=114 |pages=1–164}}</ref>

